th their hands<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attainments</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">First Attainment: Soul Gem</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation<br /> <br /> The very first Attainment makes Immortal worthy this title. During his initiation he creates phylactery, which becomes vessel for his soul, while his body becomes a mere puppet for it to command. This gives a number of benefits:<ul><li>Puppet body does not age and is are immune to all natural illnesses and diseases.</li> <li>Puppet body regenerates slowly, healing one point of Bashing damage every two minutes, one point of Lethal damage every 8 hours, and one point of Aggravated damage every day.</li> <li>Puppet body regrows lost limbs and organs as well, regrowing a lost limb in two months and a destroyed organ in weeks.</li> <li>Puppet body is able recover from death, coming back to life weak and injured, but alive as soon as it restores at least one point of aggravated damage.</li> </ul>However, this is not without downsides. Immortal how has it's phylactery, which is vulnerable, providing following downsides:<ul><li>If their phylactery is destroyed, Immortal instantly dies in a fashion that echoes the destruction of their phylactery.</li> <li>If their phylactery is damaged, the Immortal suffers a similar level of damage that cannot be healed except by repairing phylactery with either Matter magic or skilled and patient hands.</li> <li>If phylactery is removed from puppet body for more than a hundred feet apart, puppet body goes comatose. Immortal's consciousness still resides within phylactery, but normally lacks any sensory input.</li> <li>Phylactery now counts as permanent Soul Jar for soul of the Immortal. If soul is removed by any means from phylactery, Immortal instantly dies as if it was destroyed.</li> <li>Phylactery is considered to have Connected sympathy to all current puppet bodies.</li> <li>Immortal is not able to create a soul stone by any means, but phylactery itself is counted as one; Immortal is able to create Demesne from it, or use it as magical tool, if he wishes.\u200b</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Second Attainment: Enshrine the Spark</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Death 2, Occult 3<br /> <br /> At this point, Immortal perfects the act of creating phylactery and is able to transfer his death and the soul from one phylactery from another. By spending a scene of effort and point of Mana, Immortal creates new phylactery for his soul; he is able to instantly transfer his soul and death from old phylactery to new one by touching it. Old phylactery is still able to hold his death, and Immortal can switch phylactery as many times as he wants to. Phylactery must not have a Size over 5 or lesser than 1; it can be made of any material (most Immortals use works of art, jewelry or magical tools).<br /> <br /> ...and then I hit the writer's block and never wrote more Attainments. Will surely return later, when at least one Immortal appears in my games, but that's it for now.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>A fascinating Legacy, they probably have a deep psychological effect when they react to lethal injuries and great danger with an unnerving calm.<br /> <br /> The possibility of becoming a lich hunter if you defeated one must be a double edged sword, anyone who pulls it off would earn the caution, if not the outrage, of other Legacy members. Being both hunters of immortals and seekers of a better cycle of mortality must place them in direct conflict with the Psychopomp.<br /> <br /> Having the phylactery within 100 meters must be nerve wrecking, you need to plan carefully to make sure it isn't destroyed. Anyone who is good at Space and knows what to look for must be terrifying.<br /> <br /> I think you could build up on both the puppet angle and the immortal hunter one. An example would be a Ruling of Death that prevents healing for its duration, it would be scary for a vampire if all blood healing required a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> At high level, <i>Control Instincts</i> with instant use, advanced duration, affecting supernaturals and changing primary factor to Potency could be terrifying, allowing them to puppet others with the same ease as their normal vessel. It requires an aimed spell or touch, but its still a very powerful tool to disarm a target or turn them against their allies.<br /> <br /> They could use a Weaving of Death to make a voodoo doll, linking the damage of an item to the subject, similar to what happens with their phylactery. An example would be burning a letter in the middle of the night, which would make a blood bather suddenly be on fire.<br /> <br /> The appearances section suggests they might develop a way to Possess others or create decoy bodies that could allow them to venture beyond their phylactery's range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/me